course: dictionary
lesson: 2849
title: Dodgy: many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Dodgy» is an informal word, used a lot in the UK, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland. It is less common in the US. Its meaning changes with the thing it describes, so read the words around it: «a dodgy deal» is dishonest, «dodgy brakes» are not working well, and «The weather looks dodgy» means it is risky or uncertain.
explain: Ask yourself: is dodgy describing a person, a thing or a plan? A dodgy knee is hurt or weak. A dodgy curry is probably of poor quality. A dodgy website is one you should not trust.
explain: In stories, dodgy often warns you that a character is suspicious or that something is about to go wrong. Mason, in Texas, yelled «that line judge is sus!», and «sus» is slang for suspicious, which is close to dodgy. Words like these come from everyday talk, so a dictionary is useful when the clues are not enough.
explain: Use the swap check. «He made a dodgy deal» can become «He made a dishonest deal», which still makes sense, so dishonest is a good match. Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it fits.
fact: «Dodgy» is an informal adjective, so you will hear it in chatty talk more than in formal writing.
fact: «Dodgy» can mean dishonest or likely to be illegal, as in «a dodgy deal».
fact: «Dodgy» can mean not working well or unsafe, as in «dodgy brakes» and «a dodgy knee».
fact: «Dodgy» can mean of poor quality, as in «a dodgy haircut», or risky and uncertain, as in «The weather looks dodgy.»
fact: «A dodgy website» or «a dodgy message» can mean a scam, so be careful and do not trust it.
exercise: «He made a dodgy deal with the man in the car park.» What does dodgy mean here? | Made of wood | *Dishonest | Very cheap and generous | Funny and silly
exercise: Grandad says, «My knee's dodgy since the match.» What does he mean? | *Hurt or not working well | Full of ice cream | Painted bright blue | Very loud and noisy
exercise: Ella gets a message: «Click here to claim your free prize.» Her brother says it is a dodgy message. What does he mean? | It is written in very neat handwriting | It is a long message full of pictures | It is a message from her best friend | *It is probably a scam to avoid
test: «The weather looks dodgy, so take an umbrella.» What does dodgy mean here? | Sunny and warm | Very cold and snowy | *Risky or uncertain | Dishonest
test: Which phrase describes a thing that is not working well? | a sunny seaside walk | a bright red bicycle | a loud brass band | *dodgy brakes
exam: Mason says «that line judge is sus!» Sus is slang for dodgy, so what does dodgy mean in that sentence? | Excited and happy | *Suspicious | Heavy and wet | Tired after a long walk
